From fcc4a0fd5b734eafb4df170515038d19cbd72941 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:17:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iop: alarms follow thbase and return kernel errors; callbacks
 are never silently truncated (H-IOP6, H-IOP8, ALM-1/2)

Alarms (H-IOP6, ALM-1/ALM-2): SetAlarm/CancelAlarm used to shut the IOP down
on a duplicate pair, a zero delay, a full table, bad pointers, a callback that
did not return or returned non-zero. They now follow thbase.c / thcommon.c:
- a duplicate (callback, argument) pair is KE_FOUND_HANDLER, a full table
  KE_NO_MEMORY, a bad callback KE_ILLEGAL_ENTRY, a bad time pointer KE_ERROR
- delays below min_wait (USec2SysClock(2000)) are raised to it (zero is legal)
- an alarm leaves the queue before its callback runs: a self-cancel is
  KE_NOTFOUND_HANDLER (ALM-2, was 0) and the callback can re-arm itself
- a non-zero return reschedules at previous target + max(ret, min_wait)
- a callback that never returns (budget, fault, blocking call) is dropped and
  logged; other alarms and the IOP are unaffected

Callbacks (H-IOP8): interrupt, timer, CDVD and alarm callbacks ran with an
unchecked 100000-instruction budget and were cut off with no trace. The budget
is now 1,000,000 (kCallbackInstructionBudget) and any callback abandoned before
it returns (budget, tried to block, fault, unimplemented import) is logged once
per entry point.

Tests: the stale iop_alarm25_boundaries.inc (never compiled, clashed with the
RPC test name) is replaced by a live iop_alarm_boundaries.inc run from the
ioman test target (SetAlarm/CancelAlarm/repeat/self-cancel/re-arm/limits/hung
callback/retirement/reset). The test-only friend declarations in the
production header are now compiled only for the test targets (H-IOP14).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
